# 3장 (4판) 영어판: 퀘스트 ID -> (제목, 받을 때, 진행 중, 끝낼 때)
EN = {
"story_3_01": ("The Frozen Net",
 "The Elder sent you? About the ice creeping toward the village, I'd guess. It's true. Since this winter began it comes a hand's width a day. Fifteen years ago the northern sea froze in a single night. My son Elric was aboard Captain Cornelia's ship that day. Neither ship nor crew came home. Every night since, I've lit a lantern out on the ice. So he can see it on his way back.",
 "Hear out Oscar the fisherman.",
 "You'll come along. …Thank you. I know the waterways. Before it froze I knew that sea like my own palm. But I don't know why it froze. For fifteen years that's the thing I most wanted to know. And least wanted to know. Because once I know, I think I'll have to put the lantern out."),
"story_3_02": ("The Fish That Left",
 "Before we go, let's look at the catch. Cut a hole at the edge of the ice and drop a line. See what comes up these days. Fish are the first to know how the sea is doing. Bring me cod and salmon. Used to be an hour's work for a full basket.",
 "Catch 4 raw cod and 2 raw salmon and bring them to Oscar.",
 "Took a while, didn't it. And look at these eyes. Clouded. These came up from the deep. The shallow-water fish are gone. Means something down there has taken the shallows for itself. There's something big shut under the ice. Starving for fifteen years. …That's for later. First the ice maze. We start where the expedition outpost stood."),
"story_3_03": ("The Table Still Set",
 "The Order kept an outpost at the mouth of the ice maze. There was a watch on duty the night the sea froze. Not one of them got out. The Elder said it in the prologue: one day you'd see what happens when a guardian is touched without a Gate. This is it. I don't know ice. Oscar does. Go with him. And bring back exactly what you see.",
 "Find the outpost in the ice maze and examine what is left inside, with Oscar.",
 "Spoons still in their hands. No time even to run. The Elder called it 'backlash'. What comes all at once when a seal gives. They didn't die fighting. They froze at supper. …The erased village on the mural must have gone the same way. Only without even names left behind."),
"story_3_04": ("Scratched on the Shelter Wall",
 "Deeper in the maze is where the crew took shelter. The ones who left the ship and tried to walk out over the ice. That's as far as they got. Tortured souls drift there. They're the crew. If they come at you, put them to rest. Don't hate them. See what they left on the wall. A sailor always writes something down before the end.",
 "Examine the writing on the wall of the shelter in the ice maze, and put 5 tortured souls to rest.",
 "'The scholar in the grey cloak.' That cloak again. So the route was sold. To the captain. And the crew didn't blame her. Strange ship. Even after all that. Two name tags turned up. Take them to Oscar. He's the one who has to read them."),
"story_3_05": ("Say Their Names",
 "Name tags, you say. …Give them here. No, wait. Let me breathe. (Oscar fusses with the lantern wick for a long while.) All right. Hand them over. Elric's or not, a sailor's name tag has to be read out loud. That's how the man hears his own name.",
 "Hand the 2 crew name tags to Oscar.",
 "Hassan. And Mare. I know both names. Hassan mended nets well and Mare couldn't sing. (Oscar calls both names out loud toward the ice.) …Not Elric. I can't tell whether that's a mercy. As long as no tag turns up, I can keep lighting the lantern. Ask the archivist girl to write them down. Hassan and Mare."),
"story_3_06": ("Spinefish Soup",
 "They say that deep in the maze your lungs freeze just from breathing. It's the soup the outpost crew were eating. The recipe was on the back of the duty roster. Boiled with spinefish, it warms you from the inside. I'll make six bowls. As much as the six at that table never finished. Please bring me the ingredients.",
 "Bring 6 spinefish and 4 bowls of mushroom stew.",
 "Done. With this you can go down to where the Mother of the Maze is. Oscar says she's a deep-sea fish shut under the ice and starved. Before the maze existed she was only a fish of the deep. The ice shut her in, and hunger made her grow. She's a victim of that night too."),
"story_3_07": ("Lanterns of the Deep",
 "It's pitch dark under the maze. My lantern won't do. Catch anglerfish. The lure on their heads is the only light that won't go out under the ice. Jellyfish will block the way. Bring me one lure. …So the ones in the deep keep lanterns lit too. Whatever it is they're waiting for.",
 "Defeat 2 anglerfish and 3 abyssal scyphoids, and bring back 1 esca.",
 "This is it. This light will do. But you saw something odd? The anglerfish all held their lures the same way. Toward the middle of the maze. …Bait. The big one uses the little ones' lights as bait. To eat whatever comes to the light. Whatever comes to a lantern."),
"story_3_08": ("Cracking Ice",
 "Oscar has gone into the maze alone. He heard a voice from a crack in the ice. 'Father,' it said. Elric's voice, he says. I heard it too. I told you in Chapter 1. I followed my mother's voice down and… it wasn't my mother. Please hurry. He needs to hear that from someone.",
 "Put to rest the 3 tortured souls holding Oscar at the crack in the ice.",
 "(Oscar is sitting slumped on the ice.) …I know. Once I got close I knew. Elric never called me 'Father'. He called me 'old man'. Since he was twelve. That was something else wearing his voice. The archivist girl said she'd been fooled as well. …We wanted to be fooled. Both of us."),
"story_3_09": ("The Mother of the Maze",
 "The Mother of the Maze. She uses the voices of the souls she's swallowed as bait. Elric's voice came out of her belly too. Which means she ate Elric. Oscar knows it. He says he's coming anyway. Take him as far as the door, no further. Open the Memory Gate and put her to rest. She is only starving. She still has to be put to rest.",
 "Open the Memory Gate and put the Mother of the Maze to rest.",
 "When she fell she gave up every voice. Dozens of them saying their own names at once. And among them, one. 'Elric. Oscar's son.' Just as the captain used to call him. A name tag came out. And a frozen key. The ghost ship's. …I'll tell Oscar myself. That's for someone who has done his own waiting."),
"story_3_10": ("The Graveyard of Ships",
 "Past the maze lies a graveyard of ships. More than one vessel froze that night. Sharks and great eels circle between the hulls. Clear a way. You'll find a diver's helmet there. Order property, lost on the expedition twenty years ago. You need it to get under the ghost ship.",
 "Defeat 3 maws and 1 eel in the graveyard of ships.",
 "You found the helmet. And did you see? Every prow in that graveyard points one way. North. Those ships weren't running. They were going to save the captain's ship. Fishermen. Oscar will know a good many of those names. …He'll be asking himself why he didn't go out that night. I know that question."),
"story_3_11": ("The Ship Where No One Dies",
 "The ghost ship. Fifteen years in the ice's jaws. The sails haven't even rotted. The captain is holding it that hard. Go aboard and read the ship's law and its roster. Know what kind of person the captain is before you fight her. We learned that in Chapter 2.",
 "Find the ghost ship and examine the articles on the mast and the crew roster.",
 "'No one dies on my ship.' Three hundred signed under that one line. And the roster has no column for death. The day they boarded, the day they left, and that's all. It's a ship you can't die on. That's why they stayed on as souls. Because the captain won't let go. Keeping her law. …So the best kind of captain can become the most frightening kind."),
"story_3_12": ("The Morning Star",
 "'The thirty-two of the Morning Star.' There's an old wreck report in the Order's archive. Thirty years back. Captain Cornelia was twenty-two. Please read it with me. I think I see why that law was written.",
 "Read the thirty-year-old wreck report with Isabel the archivist.",
 "She lost her first ship and thirty-two crew to something huge from under the sea. Only she lived. After that she kept one line her whole life. No one dies on my ship. The grey cloak knew that when he went to her. He said there was 'a power that brings back what is forgotten'. That she could have her thirty-two back. …He knew exactly where it hurt most, and named his price there."),
"story_3_13": ("Souls Bound to the Captain",
 "I saw Elric's line in the roster. That she gave him a second scarf. That I waved from the dock a long time. …The captain wrote that down. For fifteen years I tried to hate her. It never took. Now I know why. Let's talk. Before you go to the captain.",
 "Talk with Oscar the fisherman.",
 "The captain and I were doing the same thing. She tied souls to a ship and I lit a lantern. Because letting go means it's truly over. …Put the captain to rest. Not out of hate. She needs the rest. She must have called three hundred names every day for fifteen years. I'll save my blame for that cloak."),
"story_3_14": ("Captain of the Frozen Sea",
 "Captain Cornelia. Open the Memory Gate. She has spent fifteen years with her anchor caught on the seal. She took the whole backlash and still didn't let the ship go. She has to be put to rest inside the Gate. Her blade is poisoned. Bring antidote. She will see you as the death come for her crew. She isn't wrong. Go anyway.",
 "Open the Memory Gate and put Captain Cornelia to rest.",
 "As she fell she called the names. Three hundred. Not one wrong. The last was Elric. Then she called thirty-two more. The Morning Star's. Only when she'd finished did she let go of her blade. What's left is a frozen logbook. Take it to the archivist. And look at the sea. It has begun to crack. It's thawing."),
"story_3_15": ("The Logbook",
 "I thawed the logbook. Slowly, over three days. Thaw it fast and the ink runs. Let's read it together. After we write down the captain's name.",
 "Read the thawed logbook with Isabel the archivist.",
 "It's written. Cornelia. And the three hundred and the thirty-two. Roster and all. This stone was tucked between the pages. Carved with a storm. And the last page has a map. The seven seals. The captain saw them at the end of that route. She must have drawn it to work out what the anchor struck. But listen. Some of these pages are stuck together. Glued, on purpose. There's a side she hid."),
"story_3_16": ("Flowers on the Ice",
 "The ice cracked and flowers came up. Snow wisteria. It only blooms on ice. When Elric was small he'd pick it and lay it on his mother's grave. Pick me just four. This year I'll lay them myself. In two places.",
 "Bring 4 flowers to Oscar.",
 "Two for my wife. Two for… Elric's place. It's only a stone I set on the ice. A marker, not a grave. Not yet. (Oscar lays the flowers and stands a long while.) The crew are still under the ice. The captain told them to go ashore and they can't. Someone has to gather them with a lantern. Mine."),
"story_3_17": ("The Song Beneath the Ice",
 "The captain said 'you may go ashore', did she. But men bound for fifteen years don't walk off at one word. They've forgotten how to leave. They're still singing under the ice. Take my lantern. Put the souls to rest and the lantern will gather them. Don't hate them. You're helping them down the gangway.",
 "Put 10 tortured souls in the ice maze to rest and gather them into the lantern.",
 "(Small lights waver inside the lantern.) …Hear that? The singing's stopped. Someone's laughing instead. Loud. 'Old man!' …It's Elric. He's in there. In the lantern. Fifteen years I lit this for him to see, and now he's come inside it."),
"story_3_18": ("A Heart That Can't Let Go",
 "The lantern's warm. First time in fifteen years. He's in here. Put it out and he goes. Where he's meant to go. Leave it lit and… he's here. Beside me. So this is what the captain did. Now I'm the captain. What do I do.",
 "Talk with Oscar the fisherman.",
 "…Then that's what I'll do. Thank you. Not for deciding for me. For standing here."),
"story_3_19": ("What the Net Brought Back",
 "The sea's begun to thaw and the nets bring up strange things. Not fish. Ship timber. New timber. Not fifteen years old, broken the day before yesterday. Pirates. The moment the ice loosened they came in after the ghost ship's treasure. Their ship was wrecked. I want to see what wrecked it. I told you the first day. Something big is shut under the ice, starving.",
 "Find the wrecked pirate ship, examine what is left on deck, and defeat 4 of the surviving pirates.",
 "Not broken. Carried off, you say. Mast and all. And the pirates wrote down what they saw. 'One sucker the height of a man.' …The wreck report from thirty years ago said the same. The Morning Star. It's that one. The one that took the captain's first ship. It was shut in when the sea froze, and we woke it by thawing the sea. That's the price of putting the captain to rest."),
"story_3_20": ("The One That Cradles Ships",
 "Nerakyss. The fishermen call it 'the one that cradles ships'. It isn't in the Chronicle. It's no guardian of a seal. Only a sea beast that has lived a very long time. But on the back of the wreck report my mother took down there are drawings. The captain's. After she came back alive she drew nothing else for ten days. Please look with me. I think I see why it takes ships.",
 "Examine Cornelia's drawings with Isabel the archivist.",
 "It's a nest. Built of ships. It cradles ships the way a bird sits on eggs. There's no malice in it. It's simply what it does. But at the very heart of that nest is the Morning Star. The captain drew it so. Down to the star on the prow. With the thirty-two still aboard. She wanted it back. With 'a power that brings back what is forgotten'. …The beast has to be put to rest. Once ships sail the thawed sea again, every one becomes nest. And we have to find the Morning Star. In the captain's place."),
"story_3_21": ("The Bait Boat",
 "It doesn't chase people. It chases ships. So we call it up with a ship. We'll float an empty boat. When it rises to cradle it, that's the one time it shows itself above water. Get me an oak boat. And raw cod to line the bottom. The old saying is it smells a boat before it chooses. It likes one a fisherman has sailed. …Mine would be best, but Elric sailed in that one.",
 "Bring 1 oak boat and 6 raw cod to Oscar.",
 "Good. I'll set her afloat. Named her too. A sailor doesn't launch a boat without a name. She's the Evening Star. Because she goes to fetch the Morning Star. (Oscar pushes the boat out and watches a long time.) When it comes up, I throw the harpoon. For the boat I never took out fifteen years ago."),
"story_3_22": ("To Fetch the Morning Star",
 "The Evening Star is afloat beside the wrecked pirate ship. It will come back to where it rose once. The archivist says Nerakyss isn't bound to a seal, so it can't be called inside a Gate. You fight it as it is, out on the thawing sea. When its arms wrap the boat, that's your opening. Strike the arms first. It isn't angry. It thinks someone's taking a ship meant for its nest. It still has to be put to rest. The captain couldn't do it in thirty years.",
 "Put Nerakyss the kraken to rest in the waters by the wrecked pirate ship. (Deal at least 10% of its max health)",
 "As it sank it opened its arms. Let go of everything it held. Ships came up. Hundreds. Thirty years old, a hundred years old. And one with a star on the prow. The Morning Star. Not even rotted. Because it had been held. …The thirty-two were still on deck. Just as the captain drew them. Their names have to be called. From the list she had written down. Fetch the archivist."),
"story_3_23": ("The Pages Glued Shut",
 "I got the glued pages apart. With steam. It's the side the captain hid on purpose. Not writing. A sketch. Under the floorboards of her cabin. She put something there. The ghost ship should be quiet now the souls have gone. Please go and bring it out. I'd come, but Mia has a fever.",
 "In the captain's cabin on the ghost ship, examine what is hidden under the floorboards.",
 "An orb? Cracked? …That's the same as the one in our archive. The orb from my mother's things. And a drawing of the stand, you say. In purple ink. In mirror writing. And a note. 'Write down what you hear.' Signed with a gloved hand. …Two people. Two people gave the captain something. One sold her the route and one gave her the orb. That's what Haru meant about the grey coin having two different faces."),
"story_3_24": ("Mia's Mirror",
 "Mia's fever has broken. And she read that whole drawing in a mirror. She reads mirror writing better than I do. Perhaps because she's left-handed. She found something odd while reading. Hear it for yourself. After I heard it I stood in front of the archive's orb for a long time.",
 "Hear from Isabel the archivist what Mia the apprentice read.",
 "The stand we call the Rune Altar. The one we've used since Chapter 1. Those five stones were never decoration. The drawing calls them 'five letters'. It doesn't say which. Whoever made it writes in the same hand as 'I rewrote this book' on the archive wall. The one who altered the Chronicle made a mirror that shows what's forgotten. Why? Why would the one who changed it try to hold on to what was lost? …I haven't told the Elder. But yesterday he was standing in front of the altar. Looking at the five stones. For a very long time."),
"story_3_25": ("Thawing Sea, Abyss Floor Two",
 "As the sea thaws, the second floor of the Spiral Abyss has opened. It was under water. The Abyss shows the memories of those who passed through. Fifteen years ago Captain Cornelia went through before she sailed. She used it as a trial to pick her crew. Please see what's left there.",
 "Clear the second floor of the Spiral Abyss.",
 "A dock, you say. The captain reading her law to the crew. And in the back row someone in a cloak. Not clapping. Hands behind his back. …He was there. He watched the ship leave. He saw three hundred people waving and sent them anyway."),
"story_3_26": ("Casting the Net Again",
 "The sea's loose. Fish are back in the shallows. I cast a net for the first time in fifteen years. My hands remembered. Come and eat. Grilled cod. Done the way Elric liked it. Salt and nothing else.",
 "Talk with Oscar the fisherman.",
 "How is it. …I've found something new to do at night. I hung a lamp on the dock. Not my lantern, a dock lamp. For anyone coming in. A light I used to keep for one person weighs less when it's lit for anybody. And one thing I want to ask you. That storm. The one that looked into the captain's ship. I went inside it once myself, when I was young. We'll talk about it another time. When my heart has settled a little more."),
"story_3_27": ("The Map of the Seven Seals",
 "The sea has thawed. …Well done. Truly. There was a map in Cornelia's logbook, I hear. With the places of the seven seals. Give it here. That is something the Order must keep. The seals are rotting. As you saw in Chapter 2. Now we must inspect them one by one. I will come with you myself.",
 "Hand the map of the seven seals to Elder Erwin.",
 "(The Elder takes the map. His gloved hand shakes. Whether from the map or from the sea outside the window, you can't tell. He sits with his back to it. It is the only room in the Order with a view of the sea.) Thank you. A thousand… no. I have waited a long time. Let us go and see to the seals. The first is the forge in hell. …Was there nothing else in the captain's logbook? A note, say. No. I see. Of course."),
}
